== Introduction to D.B
 $X $ smooth projective variety over $CC $, and $ dim X = n $ complex: $  0 -> cal(O)_(X) limits(arrow.r.long)^(d = partial) Omega^(1)-> ... -> O m e g a^(n)-> 0  $ there is a filtration of the cotangent sheaf: $  F^(0): 0 -> cal(O)_(X) limits(arrow.r.long)^(d = partial) Omega^(1)-> ... -> O m e g a^(n)-> 0  $ $  F^(1): 0 -> Omega^(1)-> ... -> Omega^(n)-> 0  $

 let $ G r^(p)_(F)#underline[Omega]_(X)^(dot)= Omega_(X)^(p)$

$ E_(1)^(p,q)= bb(H)^(q)(X,#underline[Omega]_(X)^(p)) => H^(p + q)(X,CC) $

*Definition 1.*  If $ cal(O)_(X)-> #underline[Omega]_(X^(0)) $ is quasi-isomorphism, then $ X $ is Du Bois.

*Proposition 1.* _property of Du Bois

  +  klt $=> $ rational singularity $=> $ Du Bois

 klt $=> $ log canonical $=> $ Du Bois
  +  A fibration $ cal(X) -> B $ such that $ cal(X)_(b) $ is D.B for all $b $. If $ cal(X)_(B_(0)) $ has $ S_(k) $ condition, then so is any $ cal(X)_(b) $
  + $ R^(q)f_(*)cal(O)_(X) $ is locally free and compatible with case change.
