 *Higher Du Bois*
*Definition 2.* Shen-Veriketesh-Vo Fix $ p in NN $, $X $ is $p $-Du bois if $X $ is semi-normal, and

  + $ h^(0)(#underline[Omega]_(X)^(k))-> #underline[Omega]_(X)^(k) $ is quasi-isomorphism for $ 0 <= k <= p $ (pre-$ p $-D.B.)
  + $ C o d i m(X_(s i n g),X)>= 2 p + 1 $
  + $ h^(0)(#underline[Omega]_(X)^(k))limits(arrow.r.long)^(tilde) #underline[Omega]_(X)^([k ]) $

*Definition 3.*  $X $ is $p $-rational singularity if $X $ is normal and

  + $ C o d i m(X_(s i n g),X)> 2 p + 1 $
  +  For log resolution $ f : hat(X) -> X $, and exceptional divisor $E $, there is $ R^(i)f_(*)(Omega_(X)^(K)(log E))= 0 $ for $ forall i >= -, 0 <= k <= p $ (pre-$ p $-rational)

_Remark 1._ some results

  +  And $ p $-rational $ => $ $ p $=Du bois.
  +  In lc I $ p - D B =>(p - q) $-rational
  +  In Non lc I $ p - D B(p - q) $-rational

== Singularity of secant varieties
 Secant varieties $ Sigma_(k) $ of a variety $X arrow.r.hook bb(P)^(N)$ is defined as union of $k $-planes generated by points in $X $.

_Remark 2._  For $ X arrow.r.hook bb(P)^(N) $ by $ | L | $, if $L $ hhas insufficient positive, then degenerate: $ dim Sigma_(k) < $ expected. (expecte $ dim Sigma^(k)= k +(k + 1)n $)

 Example: consider $ bb(P)^(2)arrow.r.hook bb(P)^(5) $, then $ Sigma $ is a hypersurface.

_Remark 3._  Assume that

*Theorem 1.* _Wlley,Vermeire $ Sigma $ is normal. _

*Theorem 2.* _Chou-S

  - $ Sigma $ has worst D.B.
  - $ Sigma $ is C.M. if and only if $ h^(1)(X,cal(O))= ...= h^(n - 1)(X,cal(O))= 0 . $
  - $ omega^(G R)_(X)tilde.equiv omega $ if and only if $ h^(n)(X,cal(O))= 0 $
